## Page templates

### ADR (`decisions/NNNN-name.md`)

```
# ADR NNNN — Decision title

Status: Proposed | Accepted | Superseded by NNNN | Deprecated
Date: YYYY-MM-DD
Owner: <role or person>
Ticket: <tracker ID, e.g. ABC-1234>   # the decision's home in the tracker — link both ways

## Context
What problem is this solving? What constraints?

## Decision
The chosen approach in 2-3 sentences.

## Consequences
What this enables. What it forecloses. Known costs.

## Alternatives considered
Brief, with why each was rejected.

## References
Links to code, related ADRs, external docs.
```

### Tribal note (`tribal/<slug>.md`)

```
# <The gotcha, in one line>

Date: YYYY-MM-DD
Ticket: <tracker ID if there was one>

## What
The non-obvious fact. What surprised you.

## Why
The underlying reason — so the next person trusts it.

## Reference
Code path, commit, trace, or incident that proves it.
```

### Service (`services/<name>.md`)

```
# Service: <name>

One-line purpose.

## Responsibilities
Bulleted. Boundaries: what it does AND does not do.

## Contract
APIs, events emitted/consumed, schemas, dependencies on other services.

## Operational
Health endpoint. Metrics. Logs. Failure modes. Recovery.

## Code home
Repo + path. Main entry point.

## Known limitations
Things to fix or watch.
```

### Theme (`themes/T<n>-<slug>.md`)

```
# T<n> — <Theme name>

Stream: <id>
Calendar: <range>
Status: Not started | In progress | Complete | Blocked

## Goal
One sentence — the checkpoint we're building toward.

## Checkpoint criteria
Bulleted, testable.

## Tickets
Tracker issue links. Status. Owner stream.

## Dependencies
Theme T<x> must complete before this can start. T<y> can run in parallel.

## Risks
Known unknowns. Mitigations.

## References
Relevant ADRs, services, requirements.
```

### Role (`roles/<name>.md`)

```
# Role: <name>

## Mission
One sentence.

## Owns
What artifacts/decisions this role is responsible for.

## Boundaries
What this role does NOT do. Who it hands off to.

## Inputs at session start
What context this role needs.

## Output format
Expected deliverables (MR, issue, ADR, etc.).

## Tools
Which tools/skills are appropriate.

## Handoff
Who picks up after this role completes a unit of work.
```

## Wiki maintenance verbs (skill `wiki`)

- `propose` — any role opens a wiki PR when they learn something durable (mid-work gotcha → `tribal/`, architectural call → `decisions/`, or post-merge).
- `ingest` — Pull a raw source into the wiki, summarized + cross-linked.
- `lint` — Maintainer-only: scan for stale claims, broken links, contradictions.
- `query` — Read-only Q&A against the wiki for any role.

See `.claude/skills/wiki/SKILL.md` for invocation details.

## Conventions

- **Markdown only.** No HTML except where Markdown can't express it.
- **Relative links.** `[X](../services/x.md)` — no absolute URLs to this repo.
- **Code references with file paths.** `path/to/file.go:42` style.
- **Dates in ISO**: `2026-05-04`. Convert relative dates to ISO when writing.
- **No emojis** unless explicitly requested.
- **No marketing language.** Plain technical English.

